OpenMVS 2.4.0: TImage::sample reads the image with the output pixel type.

Backport of the Types.inl hunk of upstream commit eeedab7 ("texture: fix
corner case in global seam leveling logic", 2026-02-27, after v2.4.0).
v2.4.0 passes INTERTYPE as the input type to Sampler::Sample, so sampling an
8-bit RGB image as float Color reads 12 bytes per pixel as floats. Local seam
leveling samples patch borders this way, which fills TextureMesh atlases with
black blobs and saturated red/green/blue specks.

Source: https://github.com/cdcseacave/openMVS (AGPL-3.0), same license as
the OpenMVS sources it applies to.

diff --git a/libs/Common/Types.inl b/libs/Common/Types.inl
index 765db20..b858d0e 100644
--- a/libs/Common/Types.inl
+++ b/libs/Common/Types.inl
@@ -2398,7 +2398,7 @@ template <typename TYPE>
 template <typename SAMPLER, typename INTERTYPE>
 INTERTYPE TImage<TYPE>::sample(const SAMPLER& sampler, const TPoint2<typename SAMPLER::Type>& pt) const
 {
-	return Sampler::Sample< INTERTYPE, INTERTYPE, TImage<TYPE>, SAMPLER, TPoint2<typename SAMPLER::Type> >(*this, sampler, pt);
+	return Sampler::Sample< TYPE, INTERTYPE, TImage<TYPE>, SAMPLER, TPoint2<typename SAMPLER::Type> >(*this, sampler, pt);
 }
 
 // convert color image to gray
